From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] xam: serverless Xbox Live stand-in for co-op networking

With --net_mode lan/direct (off by default, no change otherwise):
- XamUserGetSigninState/Info report a Live sign-in (2) and XamUserCheckPrivilege
  grants everything (--net_live_signin), so Crackdown 2's Live-only Multiplayer
  menu opens instead of "no Xbox Live multiplayer privileges".
- WSARecvFrom supports overlapped receives (WSA_IO_PENDING + host poll thread),
  WSASendTo completes its OVERLAPPED, WSAGetOverlappedResult is implemented.
  The game's Live engine (guest sub_82C7B680) needs a pending receive; the old
  stub made engine creation fail (0x807A100A) and Quick Match crash on a null
  engine at 0x838015CC.
- coop_live_sessions.cpp: hosts fill XSESSION_INFO (id, key, our XNADDR) on
  XSessionCreate and answer XSessionSearch(Ex) and XNetQosLookup probes over UDP
  guest port 1003; searches go to the configured peers (direct) or broadcast.

---
diff --git a/include/rex/kernel/xam/coop_live_sessions.h b/include/rex/kernel/xam/coop_live_sessions.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..55632e6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/rex/kernel/xam/coop_live_sessions.h
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+// Serverless stand-in for Xbox Live matchmaking (sessions, search, QoS) between
+// co-op instances (--net_mode lan/direct). Hosts answer search and QoS probes
+// on guest UDP port 1003 (mapped with --net_port_offset like the game's ports).
+#pragma once
+#include <cstdint>
+
+namespace rex::kernel::xam::coop_live {
+
+bool Enabled();
+void SetContext(uint32_t user_index, uint32_t id, uint32_t value);
+bool GetContext(uint32_t user_index, uint32_t id, uint32_t* value);
+void SetProperty(uint32_t user_index, uint32_t id, uint32_t size, uint32_t value_ptr);
+// XGI 0x000B0010: a host session gets a fresh id/key and our XNADDR written to
+// its XSESSION_INFO and is advertised; a joined session's info is left as is.
+void SessionCreate(uint32_t obj_ptr, uint32_t flags, uint32_t public_slots,
+                   uint32_t private_slots, uint32_t user_index, uint32_t session_info_ptr);
+void SessionDelete(uint32_t obj_ptr);
+void SessionJoin(uint32_t obj_ptr, uint32_t count);
+void SessionModify(uint32_t obj_ptr, uint32_t flags, uint32_t public_slots, uint32_t private_slots);
+// XGI 0x000B0016/0x000B001C: asks every peer, writes XSESSION_SEARCHRESULT_HEADER.
+void Search(uint32_t num_results, uint32_t num_ctx, uint32_t ctx_ptr, uint32_t results_buffer_size,
+            uint32_t results_ptr);
+// NetDll_XNetQosListen / XNetQosLookup.
+uint32_t QosListen(uint32_t kid_ptr, uint32_t data_ptr, uint32_t data_size, uint32_t flags);
+uint32_t QosLookup(uint32_t count, uint32_t addrs_ptr, uint32_t kids_ptr, uint32_t event_handle,
+                   uint32_t out_qos_ptr);
+
+}  // namespace rex::kernel::xam::coop_live
